: start 2018-07-20 (since 17 Oct minus 89 days = 20 July? Let's compute: Oct17 - 89 days. Oct 17 - 16 = Oct1? Wait subtract date. July20 to Oct17 inclusive: July 20-31=12, Aug31, Sep30, Oct17 total 12+31+30+17=90. Yes). Condition >= 2018-07-20 00:00 and < 2018-10-18 00:00. Good.\n\nNeed maybe if max timestamp NULL, comparison null count 0. Fine.\n\nBut note schema \"orders order_purchase_timestamp\" exists. Use cast date. PostgreSQL syntax MAX(timestamp)::date - INTERVAL. Need parentheses: (SELECT MAX(order_purchase_timestamp)::date - INTERVAL '89 days' FROM orders). Since date - interval yields timestamp. Good.\n\nPotential issue alias count? use AS order_count. Fine.\n\nOutput direct SQL. \n"},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":2882,"completion_tokens":627,"total_tokens":3509,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":2688},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":551},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":2688,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":194},"system_fingerprint":"bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}